<custom_item>
  type                     : AUDIT_POLICY_SUBCATEGORY
  description              : "1.0016 - MSSRV - Ensure 'Audit PNP Activity' is set to include 'Success'"
  info                     : "This policy setting allows you to audit when plug and play detects an external device."
  solution                 : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to include Success :

Computer Configuration\Policies\Windows Settings\Security Settings\Advanced Audit Policy Configuration\Audit Policies\Detailed Tracking\Audit PNP Activity

Impact:

Enabling this setting will allow a user to audit events when a device is plugged into a system. This can help alert IT staff if unapproved devices are plugged in.

Advanced audit logging will generate additional events when this feature is enabled."
  reference                : "NIST 800-53r5|AU-3 AU-3(1) AU-7 AU-12"
  see_also                 : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type               : AUDIT_SET
  value_data               : "Success" || "Success, Failure"
  audit_policy_subcategory : "Plug and Play Events"
</custom_item>

