<custom_item>
  type                     : REGISTRY_SETTING
  description              : "1.0271 - MSSRV - Ensure 'Notify antivirus programs when opening attachments' is set to 'Enabled'"
  info                     : "This policy setting manages the behavior for notifying registered antivirus programs."
  solution                 : "To establish the recommended configuration via GP, set the following UI path to Enabled :

User Configuration\Policies\Administrative Templates\Windows Components\Attachment Manager\Notify antivirus programs when opening attachments

Note: This Group Policy path is provided by the Group Policy template AttachmentManager.admx/adml that is included with all versions of the Microsoft Windows Administrative Templates.

Impact:

Windows tells the registered antivirus program(s) to scan the file when a user opens a file attachment. If the antivirus program fails, the attachment is blocked from being opened."
  reference                : "NIST 800-53r5|SI-3"
  see_also                 : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  value_type               : POLICY_DWORD
  value_data               : "3"
  reg_key                  : "HKU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Attachments"
  reg_item                 : "ScanWithAntiVirus"
  reg_option               : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
  reg_include_hku_users    : "S-1-5-21-*"
</custom_item>

